nodecode-ledgerline is a rewrite of Adolanium's Adolanium/hermes-ledgerline:

  https://github.com/Adolanium/hermes-ledgerline
  commit a89efceab1ff5eb0cc3f58c0482c0f1d368a6d1b
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Adolanium (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the ledger itself. The original is one JavaScript file for
Hermes Desktop that reads the gateway's session and analytics routes, prices
each session from what the gateway recorded, and draws spend by day, model and
helper task, a per-session token split, budgets, recommendations, an
on-request audit and a live pane. This cell keeps the numbers and the
questions: one read over the event log this organism keeps, added up in Lisp
into a range summary, a per-session receipt and a budget line, as three tools
the model calls and one command the operator types. No price list is
reimplemented: a round the gateway could not price stays unknown here too.

What was left out, and why: the desktop surface (the page, the statusbar chip,
the live turn pane, the six translation bundles) is Hermes Desktop's own
window dressing and has no meaning outside that app; the session browser
(title search, sort by tools or failures, profile merging, clickable receipts
and file paths) is not rebuilt, since Nodecode's own session list is the one
that browses sessions; budget alerts through a messaging platform and spend
reports as cron jobs are left to Nodecode's channels and cron cell; and the
explain/audit model calls are not ported, because the model calling
ledger_session already has the receipt in hand and can say what it means.
